Incident 2026-10-01: the daemon (pid 2492906, build 3dd3d4ce, started 2026-09-28) was killed at 07:14:47 AEST mid-webhook-flood (516 webhooks in the final 4 minutes, concurrent with the 07:05 briefing cron turn). Kill signature: last daemon.log line complete, stderr dup2'd into daemon.log shows no OCaml fatal, no coredump, no shutdown lines — external SIGKILL class. No OOM/kill journal evidence survives: journald storage is volatile on this host and journald restarted at 09:01:30 wiping the window; dmesg is restricted; auditd inactive. earlyoom is running (-n: no dmesg); kernel OOM killer or earlyoom during the morning's memory pressure (load ~16, 30G zram in use) is the most probable killer.

Impact: GitHub webhook deliveries and all connectors silently stopped for ~15h. The orphaned EC child kept running (looked 'alive' to naive checks) while nothing served. B823's takeover only acts when someone explicitly runs service start; nothing restarts a dead daemon on its own.

Decisions:
- Add a supervisor for the daemon (systemd --user unit with Restart=on-failure, or an in-clawq babysitter) so an OOM/kill leads to restart within seconds, and the B823 stale-lock takeover lets the replacement win the lock cleanly.
- The heartbeat file already gives perfect liveness signal for any external watchdog; the unit/Watcher just needs to act on it.
- Document the earlyoom interaction: the daemon is a plausible OOM victim during webhook floods; consider memory guardrails (cap in-flight webhook processing) as follow-up if RSS spikes are confirmed.

Acceptance criteria:
1. `clawq service enable` (or install command) installs a systemd --user unit (or documented equivalent) with Restart=on-failure and after=network-online.
2. Kill -9 the daemon in a test; it is back within 30s, lock/pid/heartbeat consistent, EC respawned per B828.
3. Webhook listener accepts deliveries immediately after restart (curl smoke test).
4. Docs updated (service supervision section).

Decision (2026-11-02 batch): independent service lane. Verified systemd template already has Restart=on-failure but cmd_install ignores systemctl errors and leaves existing daemons unmanaged; WatchdogSec lacks an evident notification contract. Complete production supervision/adoption semantics and verify SIGKILL recovery using an isolated scratch daemon, never kill the user daemon for testing. Serialize build/test commands centrally.

Completed: commits8c5fd720+b4e7c204+6db13bc1 merged as e9f75757 after independent scoped PASS of logging/EC, actual ownership, bounded application readiness and transient PID-publication race. Linux unit Type=exec/Restart=on-failure/RestartSec=5/control-group; install explicitly adopts manual daemon, lifecycle failures nonzero, daemon.log/rotation/EC preserved, no sd_notify watchdog. Real x-p35 scratch-unit SIGKILL recovery6.141s with new EC and matching lock/PID/heartbeat/signed webhookHTTP200; controlled500ms publication install/start/restart passed. Coordinator combined quick7801/62.274s and remote fulltree fmtPASS. Stable production install/adoption remains an operator deployment action; scratch tests did not change real user daemon.